  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The atomic number of Platinum is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>78</mn></math>. Platinum belongs Nickel group, and it is 5d series element. Electronic configuration of Platinum is<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mn>6</mn></msup><mn>3</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mn>6</mn></msup><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>10</mn></msup><mn>4</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mn>6</mn></msup><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>10</mn></msup><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mn>14</mn></msup><mn>5</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mn>6</mn></msup><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>9</mn></msup><mn>6</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></math></p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mmultiscripts><mi>Pt</mi><mprescripts></mprescripts><mn>78</mn><none></none></mmultiscripts><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi>Xe</mi></mfenced><mn>4</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mn>14</mn></msup><mn>5</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>9</mn></msup><mn>6</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></math> (Exceptional electronic configuration)",
